        <mxCell id="c89" value="Orange fill: the Furniture accounts" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="436" y="810" width="340" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c90" value="&lt;i&gt;The 85 Furniture items share one revenue, one cost of goods sold and one inventory account, so the ItemGroup selects the accounts. The orange rows hold the AccountID that Item stores and the account number the memo uses. Crow&#x27;s feet, in the notation of Chapter 3, are computed from the data. The trace names a posting&#x27;s document by type and by the key of its header (SourceDocumentID) and of its line (SourceLineID): each invoice line is named by one row of the ledger and each shipment line by two rows; the rows that post a whole document leave SourceLineID blank, so at the ledger end a line is optional.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="840" width="860" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
